00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:06.690
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:07.110
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:07.900
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:08.980
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:09.360
<b><i>#ENCODERGASM PRESENTS</i></b>

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:11.900
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.240
<b><i>#ENCODERGASM PRESENTS</i></b>

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:20.240
<i>toki ga mirai ni susumu to dare ga kimeta no da?</i>

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:20.240
<b>Who decided that time should move forward towards the future?</b>

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:26.830
<i>rakuin o kesu inochi ga rekishi o kakinaosu</i>

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:26.830
<b>The lives that will erase these brands will rewrite history</b>

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:34.840
<i>utsukushii tsurugi wa hito to hito tsunagete</i>

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:34.840
<b>People are connected by beautiful, double-edged swords</b>

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:44.770
<i>meguri kuru setsuna sa kanashimi wo aratte</i>

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:44.770
<b>Our coming anticipation will wash away our sadness</b>

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:53.780
<i>anata to no aida ni inochi aru katachi wo</i>

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:53.780
<b>With you, between us, life is formed</b>

00:00:53.780 --> 00:01:05.120
<i>Kono hoshi ni sasageru ai to iu shirushi de</i>

00:00:53.780 --> 00:01:05.120
<b>With the proof called "love" that we offer to this planet</b>

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:06.080
<i>TURN</i>

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:06.580
<i>TURN-A</i>

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:07.580
<i>TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:08.080
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:08.500
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:09.500
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:10.210
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:13.590
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:14.090
<i>TURN</i>

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:14.590
<i>TURN-A</i>

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:15.590
<i>TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:16.090
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:16.510
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:17.510
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.180
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:20.680
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:27.060
<b>The Forgotten Past</b>

00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:37.240
Will you be able to take it at night?

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:40.010
We should be, as long as we use a longer exposure time.

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:43.360
Laura's doll should be on the move. I'm heading to the communications room.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:54.460
Those are the Royal Guard's mobile suit SUMOs.

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:58.250
You seem to have quite a magnificent mobile suit yourself.

00:01:58.610 --> 00:02:00.880
That one's only a prototype.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:03.140
It's a fantastic mobile suit.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:08.020
Yes. Laura's mobile suit is quite special. But unfortunately...

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:13.340
Here comes the Militia!

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:16.640
<i>They put the names of produce and book shops on the sides of the vehicles.</i>

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:24.290
They're trying to go unnoticed.

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:28.750
But how are they going to smuggle those Kapool suits into the city!?

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:30.030
That's it!

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:34.450
Don't ruin my field, alien scum!

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:49.640
<i>Loran!</i>

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:51.050
Miss Kihel!

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.150
Where's Lord Guin?

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:55.270
He's on his way to the castle.

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:57.860
Why are we waiting here?

00:02:57.860 --> 00:02:59.860
Shouldn't you be off with Lord Guin?

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:02.530
You're planning a surprise attack with only two Kapools?

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:07.010
Of course not! When we move out, six more will arrive from the rear to back us up.

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:10.120
These ball mechanical dolls are more maneuverable. It'll be fine.

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:12.710
Loran, make sure you follow the plan.

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:13.460
Later.

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:15.190
Milady, this isn't going to work!

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:16.540
<i>Oh, shut up.</i>

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:25.640
What?!

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:29.100
- Go away!
- Stay away from Nocis!

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:32.520
A civilian resistance? Did Guin organize this?

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.560
Where's Her Majesty Dianna?!

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:41.860
This seems to be some kind of unexpected joke.

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:45.530
I'm confident that the majority of our citizens follow my lead with dignity.

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:48.660
However, there will always be a few bad apples.

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:51.470
That's how it is on the moon as well.

00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:55.780
Wherever there are people, it will always be the same, even in the past.

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:58.460
What's wrong?

00:03:58.460 --> 00:03:59.460
<i>It's the Militia!</i>

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:04.840
Take us to Bostonia Castle!

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:08.310
Pardon me!

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:11.730
Just what are you planning, Guin Rhineford?!

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:12.980
Roger that.

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:14.980
This limousine is too much of a giveaway.

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:16.230
We'll have to get out and change our route.

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:18.730
You mean I'll have to walk...?

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:20.150
<i>I refuse!</i>

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:21.980
But it sounds interesting.

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:24.360
Princess...?

00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:27.150
Sir Guin, please lead the way.

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:31.860
We've come here from all the way up there...

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:40.160
Please put your trust in me, Dianna Soriel.

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:42.920
I'll trust you.

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:45.880
Those dang mechanical dolls made it just in time...

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:48.890
Still no report from the city about that woman's capture!?

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:51.410
We can't wait around here for reinforcements!

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:53.260
All troops--

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:58.790
<i>The mechanical dolls are catching up!</i>

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:00.150
Now! Lets go!

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:02.360
- We cannot.
- Why not?!

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:07.660
If we go to your castle while things are like this, Her Majesty Dianna may be in even greater danger.

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:11.330
Bostonia Castle has been prepared for your arrival!

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:14.620
Even your Royal Guardsmen should've confirmed that.

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:18.250
No. We will head back to the <i>Soleil</i>.

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:25.460
Do you want to die here for nothing?!

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:32.060
Guin Rhineford is correct, Ambassador Miran.

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:33.600
Take my hand.

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:35.680
Thank you.

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:37.140
Shoot! Shoot!

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:41.500
<i>Lieutenant Harry! It seems Her Majesty Dianna still has yet to reach Bostonia Castle.</i>

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:42.860
Then where is she?!

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:44.680
<i>The Mustache is here!</i>

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:45.900
<i>Your orders, sir?</i>

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:49.950
Don't touch it. Just keep the soldiers occupied.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:51.830
Is that Laura's Mustache?

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:58.620
The Royal Guard... That SUMO from the airport...

00:05:58.620 --> 00:05:59.950
Or is it?

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:04.920
Don't shoot, you bastard...

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:08.040
We don't know where Her Majesty Dianna is.

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:14.060
<i>Lieutenant Harry!</i>

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:17.930
Stay back! If this one resists, I'll figure out what to do.

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:26.090
Close combat, huh?

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:27.650
He's underestimating me.

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:33.560
Stay back...

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:38.570
The Royal Guard's SUMO type is far more powerful than a FLAT.

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:40.460
What should I do...?

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:42.030
<i>Stop!</i>

00:06:42.390 --> 00:06:44.400
Stop this, Laura!

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:46.110
You too, Captain of the Royal Guard!

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:49.170
Lieutenant Harry! Her Majesty Dianna is here with us!

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:50.840
Ambassador Miran?!

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:53.010
You're saying Queen Dianna is safe?

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:56.930
Laura! You don't need to fight in Nocis City!

00:06:56.930 --> 00:07:00.080
<i>Dianna Counter mustn't be seen as a pro-war faction!</i>

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:01.190
Your Majesty!

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:03.720
It really is Queen Dianna!

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:12.150
The mustached mobile suit lost its balance.

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:19.150
I never thought the Earth would have mobile suits on the same level as the SUMO.

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:39.930
I get it!

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:46.520
The multi-monitor can view both directions?

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:48.080
And data-processing...

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:50.570
There's no data on the enemy?

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:52.500
The Royal Guard are great.

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:57.280
That Harry guy seems to consider Her Majesty Dianna very important to him too.

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:12.170
Why are we evacuating?!

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:13.050
How should I know?

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:16.840
Orders said to get at least twenty klicks away from Nocis City!

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:23.940
Does that mean the mission is a failure?

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:27.310
Loran?! Even he's...

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:38.880
As per your request, the Militia's soldiers have left Nocis City.

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:40.790
Now that that's out of the way,

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:43.660
we need to address the matter of Captain Aji's death.

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:46.750
Does the Earth truly wish to negotiate with us?

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:50.800
That was a single action carried out by a small, independent group.

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:56.140
Then can you hand over the responsible party?

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:58.380
We are currently investigating the matter.

00:08:58.380 --> 00:09:00.140
<i>Guin Rhineford...!</i>

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:02.350
<i>That's enough of that, I think.</i>

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:05.940
- I'm still covered in dirt from last night.
- <i>Right.</i>

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:09.060
Her Majesty Dianna needs rest.

00:09:09.270 --> 00:09:10.500
Of course!

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:13.440
We've already prepared the guest rooms.

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:14.850
Thank you.

00:09:15.710 --> 00:09:18.020
This way, if you'd please.

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:41.050
Move the guards to the left! To the left!

00:09:41.050 --> 00:09:46.230
Lord Guin wants to start the negotiations, so I gotta go. Sorry.

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:48.350
- Where are you going?
- I'm taking this.

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:49.640
Loran!

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:54.280
Hey, Loran's pretty stupid sometimes, don't you think?

00:09:54.500 --> 00:09:57.030
He comes through when he has to.

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:58.360
He's quite the guy.

00:09:58.590 --> 00:10:00.240
But he doesn't even do anything!

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:03.940
He could fight better with weapons, but he doesn't even want to look for any!

00:10:06.390 --> 00:10:09.040
Our reinforcements have arrived! Stop!

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:10.810
Reinforcements?

00:10:10.810 --> 00:10:12.920
Isn't that a freight train?

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:15.340
Start unloading that cargo!

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:16.550
Get off already!

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:18.040
Don't push me!

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:21.220
Loran! Lady Sochie!

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:23.680
It's old man Sid! What's up?

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:28.060
I need you to help me dig some things out of the Mountain Cycle.

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:29.690
Loran's not here.

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:33.080
I can't move my Kapool away from here.

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:37.800
We're in a ceasefire. We'd like to get the Militia as many mechanical dolls as possible.

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:38.650
Alright!

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:42.320
Then you two can come back with me on this train.

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:44.370
Huh? We're going home?

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:46.780
- No complaining.
- I don't want to go!

00:10:46.780 --> 00:10:48.370
<i>Keith!</i>

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:51.300
There you are!

00:10:51.300 --> 00:10:53.630
What happened to Fran?

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:56.160
Do you know where she ended up?

00:10:58.900 --> 00:11:00.270
Hey...

00:11:00.270 --> 00:11:01.540
Eat it.

00:11:02.690 --> 00:11:04.050
Eat it.

00:11:17.290 --> 00:11:19.400
It's still warm, and it's delicious!

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:22.320
I baked it by myself for the first time this morning.

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:23.660
All by yourself?

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:27.660
The boss broke his shoulder bone and ended up in the hospital.

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:31.460
I paid him a visit, and he said he'd be counting on me now.

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:39.960
But I don't think I'm good enough to feed the boss's wife and daughter <i>and</i> pay for his hospital bills right now.

00:11:40.610 --> 00:11:45.280
Queen Dianna has returned. Everything will be all right.

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:47.640
What should I do about my boss and his family?

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:52.760
If you, Keith of the Moonrace, can use your skills to bake bread on Earth,

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:56.370
everything will be alright.

00:11:56.370 --> 00:11:57.720
You're right.

00:12:12.690 --> 00:12:14.500
They've established a checkpoint?!

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:16.710
Halt!

00:12:17.140 --> 00:12:18.590
Where are you going?

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:21.010
The park in front of Bostonia Castle.

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:21.880
Why?

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:24.360
I'm bringing my friend her lunch.

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:27.360
Look at this delicious bread.

00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:29.740
This bike belongs to the Militia.

00:12:29.740 --> 00:12:31.680
I stole it.

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:33.980
The Militia wrecked the fields by my house.

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:35.660
Give me some of that bread.

00:12:35.660 --> 00:12:36.860
Sure.

00:12:54.640 --> 00:12:56.080
Fran!

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:57.880
How'd you find me?

00:12:58.090 --> 00:12:59.590
Keith told me where you were.

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:07.590
You want to do a report on the negotiations between the Earth and the Moonrace?

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:10.650
Don't you think everyone wants to hear about it?

00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:12.810
You mean their negotiations over the last two years?

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:15.060
We have to wait for them to make an official announcement.

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:17.660
Alright.

00:13:17.660 --> 00:13:20.070
But hey, I'm sure you'll be able to write a good report.

00:13:20.270 --> 00:13:21.630
How so?

00:13:21.630 --> 00:13:24.110
Something like, "It all went very well!"

00:13:24.110 --> 00:13:27.050
Loran, you're too dense to be a reporter.

00:13:27.050 --> 00:13:30.930
Yeah, I'm not the brightest tool in the shed...

00:13:30.930 --> 00:13:33.700
I just know enough to get by in Vicinity.

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:36.370
Her Majesty Dianna will make everything alright.

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:37.500
She can do it.

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:40.710
I heard she she came here exclusively to command her army.

00:13:40.710 --> 00:13:43.060
That's just a rumor!

00:13:43.060 --> 00:13:47.590
I didn't think the people here would be able to understand a holographic image,

00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:49.500
so I made a map instead.

00:13:50.650 --> 00:13:54.980
The green areas are the regions we believe to be uninhabited.

00:13:54.980 --> 00:14:02.020
But North Ameria's Sunbelt Zone has a mild climate and a low population density.

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:03.190
Why is that?

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:05.690
Well, the strong sunlight is bad for your body--

00:14:05.690 --> 00:14:07.110
Try again.

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:10.870
The North Amerian citizens have "memory relationships" with the land.

00:14:11.070 --> 00:14:13.490
You know the land isn't yours.

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:15.410
That's why we thought--

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:18.370
History can easily be distorted in different ways!

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:23.300
Who the hell do you think will tolerate all of you suddenly returning to Earth?!

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:24.800
Duke Erizona!

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:26.510
I don't care!

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:31.090
There's not a shred of truth to this Dark History you speak of!

00:14:31.090 --> 00:14:33.600
Then what is it that you believe?

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:37.390
You people are the ones who fled and left the Earth!

00:14:37.390 --> 00:14:38.690
We fled, you say?!

00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:43.020
My ancestors remained on Earth and worked to once again bring it back to life.

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:46.070
Your cowardly ancestors just ran away!

00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:48.400
That's awfully harsh.

00:14:54.050 --> 00:14:56.990
What are they investigating in a place like this?

00:14:59.430 --> 00:15:01.350
It's not just that WaDom...

00:15:01.350 --> 00:15:05.290
I hope Milady Sochie and Miashei won't pop up so suddenly.

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:14.010
<i>The Militia may have left Nocis, but aren't they just hiding out in these regions?</i>

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:15.850
That was Her Majesty Dianna's decision.

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:19.810
Even so, Poe, Her Majesty Dianna isn't a soldier.

00:15:19.810 --> 00:15:24.240
It's our duty to compensate for Queen Dianna's weaknesses.

00:15:24.240 --> 00:15:26.900
The Militia is getting more powerful.

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:28.690
<i>That's what a truce is used for.</i>

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:30.490
<i>- We're moving out.</i>
- Huh?

00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:33.200
Lets go back to Vicinity and check it out.

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:34.400
S-Sir!

00:15:35.930 --> 00:15:39.000
What are all those people gathering for?

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:42.540
<i>They seem to be holding some kind of banquet.</i>

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:44.490
Cheers!

00:15:45.350 --> 00:15:47.670
I hear those space guys don't eat a whole lot...

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:49.580
Eat up now!

00:16:02.660 --> 00:16:04.600
- To the White Doll!

00:16:03.830 --> 00:16:05.810
- Our great mechanical doll!

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:12.360
It's way too dangerous to let them use the Kapools out there!

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:16.690
Our first priority is the excavation at Mountain Cycle.

00:16:17.550 --> 00:16:19.580
They're being way too irresponsible.

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:21.910
I wonder if there are any WaDs nearby?

00:16:24.220 --> 00:16:26.380
<i>The mustached mobile suit is on the move.</i>

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:27.000
<i>Your orders?</i>

00:16:27.230 --> 00:16:31.370
Our mission is to monitor the troops gathered here.

00:16:33.020 --> 00:16:36.470
Deviating from the mission will only upset the Lieutenant...

00:16:39.240 --> 00:16:42.890
<i>The enemy is closing in! It's the jellyfish! The jellyfish is approaching!</i>

00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:45.650
That's not good! l can't let the enemy find the secrets we've discovered here!

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:49.390
Dianna Counter's giant biped model?

00:16:51.040 --> 00:16:52.990
Miashei, do you read me?

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:55.660
<i>You're turned up way too loud!</i>

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:57.700
So are you!

00:16:57.700 --> 00:17:01.490
Shouldn't we draw the enemy doll's attention away from here?

00:17:01.490 --> 00:17:04.340
Roger that. Let's start 'em up!

00:17:04.340 --> 00:17:07.580
Mr. Joseph! We're heading out!

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:11.000
Old man Sid, can't this thing shoot rockets?

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:14.940
We haven't tested them. You probably shouldn't try to fire them yet.

00:17:14.940 --> 00:17:17.210
Hey now, get those out of here!

00:17:19.760 --> 00:17:22.470
Joseph said these machines should be very durable, but

00:17:22.470 --> 00:17:25.510
You still don't wanna take a direct hit from a rocket or anything.

00:17:25.510 --> 00:17:28.810
We just have to keep them away from the Mountain Cycle, right?

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:29.890
Roger that!

00:17:40.840 --> 00:17:43.540
They're the same ones we saw at Nocis.

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:46.160
Just how many of this kind of suit does the Militia have?!

00:17:46.370 --> 00:17:49.410
Their numbers could be a problem, but their performance is most important!

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:53.000
We evaded them!

00:17:56.530 --> 00:17:59.020
Whoa! I dodged 'em!

00:17:59.020 --> 00:18:01.380
Sochie, you alright?

00:18:03.660 --> 00:18:06.020
There must be some weapons somewhere.

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:09.010
There's no reason this kind of mobile suit wouldn't have weapons.

00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:12.020
I found something?!

00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:14.190
It looks a bit like Vicinity, but...

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:15.690
What era is is from?

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:19.280
I'm bound to fail if I fight unarmed.

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:23.280
Milady Sochie, please don't do anything foolish!

00:18:25.640 --> 00:18:27.280
It's underground?

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:36.760
It's the White Doll!

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:42.210
This thing is going to that spot?

00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:05.840
This is... What the...?

00:19:05.840 --> 00:19:07.830
The altar house...

00:19:12.640 --> 00:19:13.960
The stones...

00:19:14.560 --> 00:19:16.580
The ground is...?!

00:19:37.330 --> 00:19:39.310
The White Doll's weapons!

00:19:44.050 --> 00:19:45.700
It crumbled?!

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:47.110
But why?

00:19:56.350 --> 00:19:58.000
Are you kidding me?!

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:00.870
Of all the weapons, these are all that's left?

00:20:01.520 --> 00:20:03.290
Damn it!

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:13.850
Sochie, you can't beat them unless you use your rockets!

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:17.100
If I don't, I won't be able to avenge Daddy!

00:20:17.100 --> 00:20:20.110
Poe! Don't waste your time on these suits!

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:21.990
They're nothing but paper tigers!

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:24.050
Well, we've got a non-paper tiger incoming!

00:20:24.050 --> 00:20:25.990
- Is that it?
<i>- It's the Mustache!</i>

00:20:25.990 --> 00:20:27.400
I can tell from its silhouette!

00:20:30.850 --> 00:20:32.840
Inputting the I-field...

00:20:32.840 --> 00:20:34.780
Is this going to work?

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:39.750
We didn't bring the capture net!

00:20:39.750 --> 00:20:41.860
I won't let you hurt the girls!

00:20:41.860 --> 00:20:43.880
Just grab it with your hands!

00:20:54.660 --> 00:20:57.860
Only a barbarian would do such a thing!

00:21:02.840 --> 00:21:04.490
Did we get it?!

00:21:04.490 --> 00:21:05.070
<i>From above!</i>

00:21:07.280 --> 00:21:10.930
Earth is no place to start a war!

00:21:10.930 --> 00:21:12.280
Damn Mustache!

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:15.070
What?!

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:19.550
Poe! Think of something!

00:21:19.550 --> 00:21:21.500
I don't know what to do!

00:21:28.240 --> 00:21:29.800
Are they running?

00:21:31.530 --> 00:21:33.510
What the heck happened here?

00:21:35.540 --> 00:21:39.190
He can be be pretty scary when he fights seriously!

00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:40.480
Sochie!

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:42.280
I know.

00:21:42.280 --> 00:21:45.990
This ball also has some kind of device which can show electrical images.

00:21:45.990 --> 00:21:48.070
It's called a television.

00:21:48.070 --> 00:21:50.580
Old man Sid told me about it.

00:21:50.580 --> 00:21:54.610
So the White Doll can use a weapon like that?

00:21:55.710 --> 00:21:59.920
Loran! That's you driving it, right? Show me your face!

00:22:05.860 --> 00:22:08.590
Queen Dianna! Queen Dianna...!

00:22:08.590 --> 00:22:11.890
I'm begging you! Earth is beautiful!

00:22:11.890 --> 00:22:13.680
It's wonderful!

00:22:13.680 --> 00:22:16.180
You can't let a war start here!

00:22:16.180 --> 00:22:19.900
I don't know what else I can do!

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:22.810
I beg of you, Your Majesty Dianna.

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b><i>Binetsu ga samenai mama</i></b>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b>As if unawoken from a slight fever</b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b><i>Utsumuku shounen no hitomi wa</i></b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b>The eyes of the boy hanging his head</b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b><i>Kokoro no umi mitsumete</i></b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b>Gaze upon the sea of his heart</b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b><i>Shizuka ni hohoenderu</i></b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b>And smile silently</b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b><i>Umare kuru mono kiete yuku mono</i></b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b>What is born, and what fades away</b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b><i>Subete wa sadame no furiko no haba</i></b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b>Are but the sway of the pendulum of fate</b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b><i>Zasetsu no yami o tsukinuke mietekuru</i></b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b>Piercing the darkness of frustration, he begins to see it</b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b><i>Sore ga hikari no shinjitsu</i></b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b>It is the reality of the light</b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b><i>Yoake totomoni wasuresareru hoshi ni sasagu</i></b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b>Together with dawn, he gives an offering to the stars that will be forgotten</b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b><i>Shijou no ai wa chiisana sono te no naka ni aru</i></b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b>History's love lies in his tiny hands</b>

00:23:40.230 --> 00:23:42.040
<i>That's Her Majesty Dianna for you!</i>

00:23:42.500 --> 00:23:45.570
<i>In order to improve relations between the people of the Earth and moon,</i>

00:23:45.570 --> 00:23:48.470
<i>she decides to hold a dance party.</i>

00:23:48.470 --> 00:23:53.190
<i>I had to attend it as Laura, the White Doll's pilot.</i>

00:23:53.190 --> 00:23:57.780
<i>Therefore, l ended up following Miss Kihel's unexpected training to become a proper lady.</i>

00:23:58.870 --> 00:24:01.460
<i>Next time, on </i>Turn-A Gundam,

00:24:01.460 --> 00:24:03.420
<i>Training to Be a Lady</i>

00:24:03.420 --> 00:24:06.740
"I'm gonna dance like the wind!"

00:24:03.500 --> 00:24:08.420
<b>Training to Be a Lady</b>
